---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';

const updated = '24 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use | Radixa Technologies"
  description="Terms governing use of the radixa.co.uk website."
  noindex
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Terms of use</h1>
        <p class="lede">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <p>
          These terms govern your use of radixa.co.uk, operated by {site.legalName}. By using the
          site you accept them. If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.
        </p>

        <h2>Informational content only</h2>
        <p>
          Everything on this website is published for general information about our services. It is
          not accounting, audit, tax, legal, financial or professional advice, and it is not a
          substitute for advice tailored to your organisation's circumstances. Nothing here creates
          a professional relationship between you and Radixa.
        </p>
        <p>
          Do not act, or refrain from acting, on the basis of content on this site without taking
          appropriate professional advice. Descriptions of accounting treatments, system capabilities
          and platform behaviour are general and may not reflect your specific version, configuration,
          licensing or reporting requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable care to keep this site accurate and available, but we make no warranty
          that it is complete, current or uninterrupted. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we
          exclude liability for any loss arising from reliance on this site. Nothing in these terms
          limits liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for any
          liability that cannot lawfully be limited.
        </p>

        <h2>Enquiries</h2>
        <p>
          Submitting an enquiry does not create a contract or oblige us to provide services. Any
          engagement is governed by a separate written agreement. Please do not send confidential
          information, personal data about other people, or material subject to a non-disclosure
          obligation through the website forms.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The content, design, text, graphics and logos on this site are owned by or licensed to
          {' '}{site.legalName} and are protected by intellectual property law. You may view, download
          and print pages for your own internal reference. You may not republish, reproduce
          commercially or systematically extract content without our written permission.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party names and links</h2>
        <p>
          SAP, S/4HANA, SAP Analytics Cloud, SAP BPC and other SAP product names are trademarks or
          registered trademarks of SAP SE. Other product and company names are the trademarks of
          their respective owners. We use them descriptively to identify the platforms we work with.
          Their use does not imply partnership, endorsement, certification or affiliation, and Radixa
          Technologies is not an SAP partner or reseller.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where we link to external websites, we do so for convenience. We do not control them and
          are not responsible for their content or their privacy practices.
        </p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          You must not misuse this site by knowingly introducing malicious code, attempting to gain
          unauthorised access, submitting automated or fraudulent enquiries, or using it in any way
          that is unlawful or that could damage or impair its availability.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. The version published on this page at the time
          you use the site is the version that applies.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and the courts of England and
          Wales have exclusive jurisdiction.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          {site.legalName} — <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
